 '{"trd_pro_factory_rack":"TRD roof rack new for 2019 and exclusive to the TRD Pro (Toyota 2019, 2020 and 2021 releases); 2022-2024 not confirmed; Trail and Venture Special Editions carry Yakima cargo baskets (Toyota 2021 release)","rear_window":"power roll-down","third_row":"optional (Limited/SR5)","roof_load":"120 lb per a reader comment on Trail4Runner citing a 2016 SR5 owner manual; not confirmed from a Toyota document, and the comment does not say whether it is the rail limit or the roof limit; confirm in the owner manual; a Toyota dealer parts page for the Genuine Toyota cross bar kit PT278-89170 gives 132 lb evenly distributed across both bars, which is a bar rating and not a roof limit, and the page lists no model years","fit_note":"Crossbar kits clamp to raised rails. TRD Pro (TRD roof rack, new for 2019) and the Trail and Venture Special Editions (Yakima basket) carry a factory rack or basket, so look at the roof first.","hitch":"integrated tow-hitch receiver and wiring harness standard on all grades per Toyota 2017, 2019, 2020 and 2021 releases; Toyota names no hitch class or receiver size in those releases; Class 3 and 2 in are not confirmed from a Toyota document, read the label on the receiver","tow":"5,000 lb maximum with 500 lb maximum tongue weight on all models (Toyota 2017, 2019, 2020 and 2021 releases)","hitch_fact":"factory receiver standard on all grades per Toyota (2017 to 2021 releases); Toyota names no hitch class","hitch_check":"Toyota lists a tow-hitch receiver and wiring harness as standard on all grades (2017 to 2021 releases), so look under the rear bumper before buying a hitch.","hitch_blurb":"Toyota lists an integrated tow-hitch receiver and wiring harness as standard on all grades in its 2017, 2019, 2020 and 2021 releases and names no hitch class, so look under the rear bumper before buying a hitch and read the label on the receiver. An aftermarket hitch never raises the vehicle rating.","tow_fact":"5,000 lb max with 500 lb tongue weight on all models (Toyota)","roof_fact":"120 lb per a 2016 SR5 owner manual figure cited by a reader; not confirmed from Toyota"}',
 'Factory raised rails on most trims; the TRD Pro has a TRD roof rack from 2019. Long generation = huge aftermarket; Toyota lists a tow-hitch receiver and wiring harness as standard on all grades, with 5,000 lb towing and 500 lb tongue weight.'),

((SELECT id FROM makes WHERE slug='toyota'),'4runner','4Runner','2025-present','6th Gen (N500)',2025,NULL,'suv',
